    "durationMs": 236738,
    "finalText": "Implementation complete and verified. The URL shortener API is built and fully tested:\n\n**What I built** (Go + chi v5.2.1 + PostgreSQL via `database/sql` with the pgx driver):\n- `main.go` — reads `DATABASE_URL`, opens the pool (with connection retry), applies migrations, serves chi on `0.0.0.0:8000` with graceful shutdown\n- `migrate.go` — embedded migration runner that applies pending `migrations/*.sql` in order, tracked in `schema_migrations` (runs on startup, so `sh start.sh` applies migrations then serves in the foreground)\n- `migrations/0001_init.*.sql` — `links` table (`id`, unique `code`, `url`, `clicks`, `created_at`)\n- `store.go` — insert with collision-retry code generation (8 chars, crypto/rand), lookup, atomic `UPDATE ... SET clicks = clicks + 1 RETURNING url` (exactly-once increment), listing by ascending `id`\n- `handlers.go` — all routes; URL validation (absolute http/https with a host), code regex `^[A-Za-z0-9_-]{4,20}$`, `422` for malformed JSON/invalid url/invalid code, `409` for duplicate custom code, `404` with `{\"error\": ...}` for unknown codes, `302` with exact `Location`\n- `start.sh` (executable, serves foreground; binary prebuilt) and a README with startup instructions\n\n**Verified end-to-end** against a live PostgreSQL: 39/39 HTTP checks passed (all endpoints, validation matrix, boundary codes 4/20 chars, duplicate → 409, redirect Location byte-identical including `&`), and a kill/restart cycle confirmed links and click counts persist (clicks: 3 → restart → still 3 → 4 after one more redirect). The database is reset to a pristine state and port 8000 is free, ready for the grader's `sh start.sh`."
  }
